# Copy to .env.local for local dev (it is gitignored).
#
# Base URL of the CatRanger FastAPI control server (`catranger serve`).
# The console's REST calls, the MJPEG <img>, and the control WebSocket all
# derive from it. If unset, the client defaults to http://localhost:8080.
#
# BUILD-TIME vs RUNTIME — important:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE is INLINED into the client bundle at `next build`.
#   Changing it requires a rebuild/redeploy. On Vercel, setting it in the
#   dashboard is also build-time — so for a hosted deploy you typically leave it
#   UNSET (the public landing needs no backend). To retarget the console without
#   rebuilding, use the in-app **Backend URL** field (Connections tab), which is
#   saved in the browser and overrides this value at runtime.
#
# For phone / LAN access, set this (or the Backend URL field) to the HOST
# machine's LAN IP (not localhost, which on a phone means the phone itself),
# e.g. http://192.168.1.42:8080 — and add that origin to `cors_origins` in
# configs/web.yaml.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:8080
